%% ALPHABETS DEMO using BALL-VISUAL-TRACKING:
# On the secondary computer (petar@deniro-pc), run the following:
$ python objtrack.py # runs the object tracker controlled with button reader for starting to store a segment 
$ python keyboard_controller.py # for controlling when to send the drawing objective ("f") and when to restart ("r")

# On the main computer, run air_drawing.py 
***************************** In case of issues **********************************   
- Check which USB port is used for Arduino-driven button:
$ cat /dev/tty[TAB]
If serial-port name is different from the one in the objtrack.py, change name in the script. 

- If serial-port access is not permitted by the machine, you'd need to add the user to the dialout group for using the 
serial ports: 
$ sudo adduser second_user dialout

- If things still don't work, you may need to install arduino:
$ sudo apt-get install arduino
